    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14482" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπρόσ-ῐτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unapproachable,
				inaccessible,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.49.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.3.18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Ti.</u>
					6.16
				</span></i>
			; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				5.20.6
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.68e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταφυγή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					19.96
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοις ἀ. παρρησία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύναμις τοῦ λόγου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Dem.Enc.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.45f
				</span></i>
			.</div>
